Upstream-Name: mos
Comment: One copyright file for every package this producer family emits --
 mosd, mos-apid, mos-mqttd and mos-mqtt-broker -- installed per package as
 /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright so that no two packages own one path.
 .
 The statically linked Rust dependencies of those binaries are not an open
 set. os/pkgs/mosd/deny.toml is the authority: it allows Apache-2.0, MIT,
 BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, Unicode-3.0 and Zlib, plus CC0-1.0 for
 tiny-keccak on one named dependency chain and for nothing else. cargo-deny
 enforces that list against the resolved graph, so a dependency under any
 other licence fails before it can reach a package. Read that file rather
 than this paragraph for the current set; this one restates it and can fall
 behind it.

